# A FREQ x RA x DEC cube whose celestial axes are pixel axes 2 and 3, with
# SIP keywords and no '-SIP' suffix (synthetic). wcslib 8.10 ACCEPTS it: SIP
# has no axis mapping, so wcspih applies the polynomial to pixel axes 1 and
# 2 (here FREQ and RA), which mixes the spectral pixel axis into the sky
# position. We refuse a SIP header whose celestial axes are not pixel axes
# 1 and 2 rather than guess (rule 7). AP/BP are given so hdr2sky injects
# nothing.
# EXPECT-GO-ERROR: SIP is defined on pixel axes 1,2 only
NOTE stricter: sip_nosuffix_cube_axes23
GRID 1 256 5 1 256 5
HEADER
NAXIS   = 3
NAXIS1  = 16
NAXIS2  = 256
NAXIS3  = 256
CTYPE1  = 'FREQ'
CTYPE2  = 'RA---TAN'
CTYPE3  = 'DEC--TAN'
CRVAL1  = 1.4E9
CRVAL2  = 180.0
CRVAL3  = 30.0
CRPIX1  = 1.0
CRPIX2  = 128.5
CRPIX3  = 128.5
CDELT1  = 1.0E6
CDELT2  = -0.001
CDELT3  = 0.001
A_ORDER = 2
A_2_0   = 1.0E-5
B_ORDER = 2
B_0_2   = 1.0E-5
AP_ORDER= 1
AP_0_0  = 0.0
BP_ORDER= 1
BP_0_0  = 0.0
